```
Reason:
In `mthca_create_srq()`, when `ib_copy_to_udata()` fails, the error path calls `mthca_free_srq()` but does not call `mthca_unmap_user_db()` to release the user doorbell that was mapped earlier. This causes a resource leak. In `mthca_destroy_srq()`, `mthca_free_srq()` is called after `mthca_unmap_user_db()`, leading to a potential use-after-free because `mthca_unmap_user_db()` accesses the `db_index` field which is part of the srq structure that gets freed by `mthca_free_srq()`.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (context && ib_copy_to_udata(udata, &srq->srqn, sizeof(__u32))) {
    mthca_free_srq(to_mdev(ibsrq->device), srq);
    mthca_unmap_user_db(to_mdev(ibsrq->device), &context->uar,
                        context->db_tab, ucmd.db_index);
    return -EFAULT;
}
```
and
```c
mthca_free_srq(to_mdev(srq->device), to_msrq(srq));
if (udata) {
    ...
    mthca_unmap_user_db(...);
}
```
Reason:
In `mthca_create_srq()`, the added `mthca_unmap_user_db()` call ensures that the user doorbell is properly unmapped before returning the error, preventing a resource leak. In `mthca_destroy_srq()`, moving `mthca_free_srq()` before the unmapping ensures that the `srq` structure is still valid when `mthca_unmap_user_db()` reads the `db_index`, thus avoiding a use-after-free. The corrected order also mirrors the error path in creation, where unmapping must happen before freeing.

